# Glossary (spec §12.1, §12.3): every term a lesson lists in `glossary` has
# `glossary-<id>` (the term) and `glossary-<id>-def` (the definition) here.

glossary-alpha = Alpha
glossary-alpha-def = How often a bluff must make the opponent fold to break even: bet / (pot + bet).
glossary-big-blind = Big blind (bb)
glossary-big-blind-def = The larger forced bet, and the unit Taful measures stacks and pots in.
glossary-blocker = Blocker
glossary-blocker-def = A card you hold that removes combos from your opponent's range.
glossary-board = Board
glossary-board-def = The community cards every player shares: flop, turn and river.
glossary-button = Button (BTN)
glossary-button-def = The dealer seat. It acts last after the flop, the best position at the table.
glossary-combo = Combo
glossary-combo-def = One exact two-card combination, such as A♠ K♠. AKs has 4, AKo 12, a pair 6.
glossary-dirty-outs = Dirty outs
glossary-dirty-outs-def = Cards that complete your draw but also improve your opponent to a better hand.
glossary-effective-stack = Effective stack
glossary-effective-stack-def = The smaller of the two stacks in a hand: the most either player can win or lose.
glossary-equity = Equity
glossary-equity-def = Your share of the pot if all cards were dealt with no more betting.
glossary-kicker = Kicker
glossary-kicker-def = A side card that breaks ties between hands of the same category.
glossary-mdf = Minimum defense frequency (MDF)
glossary-mdf-def = How often you must continue against a bet so bluffs do not profit automatically: pot / (pot + bet).
glossary-outs = Outs
glossary-outs-def = Cards that, if they come next, put you ahead.
glossary-position = Position
glossary-position-def = Acting after your opponent on a street. The player in position sees more before deciding.
glossary-pot-odds = Pot odds
glossary-pot-odds-def = The equity a call needs to break even: bet / (pot + 2 × bet).
glossary-range = Range
glossary-range-def = The set of hands a player can hold in a spot, with how often each is played.
glossary-spr = Stack-to-pot ratio (SPR)
glossary-spr-def = Effective stack divided by the pot on the flop; how committed the hand is.
